\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\vfill

\begin{keyidea}[The last word]
Every model in this book is a claim about how your data were generated. The
arithmetic will run whatever you claim. The whole craft lies in checking whether
the claim is defensible --- which is why the diagnostic chapters matter more than
the fitting ones. Fit the simple model, look hard at how it fails, and let the
failure tell you what to fit next.
\end{keyidea}
